We can think of $|x + 15|$ as the distance between $x$ and $-15$ on the real numbers line, and $|x - 19|$ as the distance between $x$ and 19 on the real number line.

[asy]
unitsize(0.2 cm);

draw((-25,0)--(25,0));
draw((-15,-0.5)--(-15,0.5));
draw((19,-0.5)--(19,0.5));
draw((4,-0.5)--(4,0.5));

label("$-15$", (-15,-0.5), S);
label("$19$", (19,-0.5), S);
label("$x$", (4,-0.5), S);
[/asy]

By the Triangle Inequality, the sum of these distances is at least $19 - (-15) = 34,$ which implies that at least one of $|x + 15|$ and $|x - 19|$ is always at least 17.  Therefore, $f(x) \ge 17.$

Note that $f(2) = 17,$ so the minimum value of $f(x)$ is $\boxed{17}.$

question:
Tangents are drawn from $(1,3)$ to the parabola $y^2 = 4x,$ at $A$ and $B.$  Find the length $AB.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

real upperparab (real x) {
  return (sqrt(4*x));
}

real lowerparab (real x) {
  return (-sqrt(4*x));
}

pair A, B, P;

P = (1,3);
A = ((7 + 3*sqrt(5))/2, upperparab((7 + 3*sqrt(5))/2));
B = ((7 - 3*sqrt(5))/2, upperparab((7 - 3*sqrt(5))/2));

draw(graph(upperparab,0,10));
draw(graph(lowerparab,0,10));
draw(interp(A,P,-0.8)--interp(A,P,1.2));
draw(interp(B,P,-1)--interp(B,P,1.5));

